<p>Say: &quot;Before we start, stand up if you're able. Roll your shoulders twice. Look at something about twenty feet away for twenty seconds — that resets your eyes after a screen block. Then sit down.&quot; Make participation explicitly optional and do not single anyone out. Keep it to one minute; announce the time so the room knows it is bounded.</p>
